title: War or Peace?
subtitle: The spring of 1918.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 28 and bol_regime = 0 and at_war = 1
priority: 40
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.peace_ok = (Q.stockholm >= 3 || Q.separate_feelers || Q.war_weariness <= 55) ? 1 : 0;
Q.army_collapse = (Q.war_weariness >= 80 && Q.army_discipline < 30) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: war_peace if peace_ok = 1; war_collapse if army_collapse = 1; war_goes_on if peace_ok = 0 and army_collapse = 0

@war_peace
on-arrival: {!
Q.at_war = 0;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -25, bolshevik: -6, soviet_democracy: 2, right_threat: -3});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3, workers: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -4);
!}

= An Armistice

The Stockholm conference and the quiet negotiations through neutral intermediaries have led to a result. Germany, with her own revolution brewing at home and her armies short of men, has agreed to an armistice on the Eastern Front: no annexations, no indemnities, with plebiscites in the disputed territories.

The war on the Eastern Front is over. The party's internationalists say that the war was ended by a socialist initiative. The Defencists do not argue.

@war_collapse
on-arrival: {!
Q.at_war = 0;
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: -10, right_threat: 10, bolshevik: 8, soviet_democracy: -2, rel_kad: -4});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: -3, middle: -2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -2, 6);
!}

= The Front Collapses

By March the army can no longer fight. The Germans attacked in February, and the front dissolved. The government has signed what it must: a peace on harsh terms, in which Russia loses Poland, the Baltic provinces and much of Ukraine.

The government is blamed for the peace, and the army for the defeat.

@war_goes_on
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {war_weariness: 4, bolshevik: 4, bread: -2});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: -1});
!}

= The War Goes On

The war on the Eastern Front is in its fourth year. The army is exhausted, but it holds the line, in a world in which the Allied offensive in the west has begun to bite. The soldiers say that there will be peace when the Kaiser falls.

The Bolsheviks and the Left are arguing for an immediate peace. The government has no answer for them.
